('edf1d3a7-4649-51b0-850a-29becb79b37d','abe478b1-f762-5c31-b8dc-91797783ddd5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','not likely to happen',null,null,'بعید، نامحتمل','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['highly/most/very unlikely It’s highly unlikely that he’ll survive.','extremely unlikely The government is extremely unlikely to change its policy.','rather/pretty/quite/fairly unlikely I may have thrown it away by mistake, but that’s pretty unlikely.','increasingly unlikely (= more and more unlikely as time passes ) It looks increasingly unlikely that the Bank of England will cut interest rates.','an unlikely possibility/prospect The most unlikely possibility was that she might resign.','an unlikely scenario/occurrence They should build a new road, but that’s an unlikely scenario.','an unlikely alliance/coalition Once he resigned as president, the unlikely coalition of former enemies fell apart.','in the unlikely event of something (= if something which is unlikely happens ) In the unlikely event of an accident, the system will automatically shut down.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Donna might be able to come tomorrow, but it’s very unlikely .","translation":"دونا ممکن است فردا بیاید، اما بعید است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000522295.mp3"},{"sentence":"The weather is unlikely to improve over the next few days.","translation":"بعید است در چند روز آینده وضعیت هوا بهبود یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638852.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s unlikely that the thieves will be caught.","translation":"بعید است که دزدان دستگیر شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000522298.mp3"},{"sentence":"In the unlikely event of a fire, passengers should move to the top deck.","translation":"در صورت وقوع آتش سوزی، مسافران باید به بالای عرشه حرکت کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000522302.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('78198436-4086-50d3-bcba-9eecff13562e','abe478b1-f762-5c31-b8dc-91797783ddd5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an unlikely place, person, or thing is strange and not what you would expect',null,null,'یک مکان، شخص یا چیز بعید عجیب است و آن چیزی نیست که شما انتظار دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['highly/most/very unlikely It’s highly unlikely that he’ll survive.','extremely unlikely The government is extremely unlikely to change its policy.','rather/pretty/quite/fairly unlikely I may have thrown it away by mistake, but that’s pretty unlikely.','increasingly unlikely (= more and more unlikely as time passes ) It looks increasingly unlikely that the Bank of England will cut interest rates.','an unlikely possibility/prospect The most unlikely possibility was that she might resign.','an unlikely scenario/occurrence They should build a new road, but that’s an unlikely scenario.','an unlikely alliance/coalition Once he resigned as president, the unlikely coalition of former enemies fell apart.','in the unlikely event of something (= if something which is unlikely happens ) In the unlikely event of an accident, the system will automatically shut down.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The birds had nested in some unlikely places .","translation":"پرندگان در جاهای بعید لانه کرده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001674.mp3"},{"sentence":"The quiet village of Brockhampton was an unlikely setting for such a crime.","translation":"دهکده آرام بروکهمپتون محیطی بعید برای چنین جنایتی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638857.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
