('6db09c75-b781-596c-936c-0bf1b4141549','8c28c71b-f03d-5a57-b915-6c94f4486a42',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to tell the public about a product or service in order to persuade them to buy it',null,null,'تبلیغ کردن (کالا، خدمت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They no longer advertise alcohol or cigarettes at sporting events.","translation":"آنها دیگر در رویدادهای ورزشی الکل یا سیگار را تبلیغ نمی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001646844.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many companies will only advertise in the Sunday paper.","translation":"بسیاری از شرکت ها فقط در روزنامه یکشنبه تبلیغ می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001646847.mp3"},{"sentence":"The inn is advertised as being from the early 16th century.","translation":"این مسافرخانه به عنوان متعلق به اوایل قرن شانزدهم تبلیغ می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001646850.mp3"},{"sentence":"Colleges and universities have found that it pays to advertise (= advertising brings good results ) .","translation":"کالج‌ها و دانشگاه‌ها دریافته‌اند که تبلیغات به صرفه است (= تبلیغات نتایج خوبی می‌آورد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001646851.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('a0aa4ae1-4d29-5f13-b295-be5fb244c292','8c28c71b-f03d-5a57-b915-6c94f4486a42',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to make an announcement , for example in a newspaper or on a poster , that a job is available , an event is going to happen etc',null,null,'اعلامیه ای مثلاً در یک روزنامه یا روی پوستر مبنی بر اینکه شغلی در دسترس است، رویدادی قرار است اتفاق بیفتد و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a poster advertising the concert","translation":"پوستری تبلیغاتی کنسرت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000793566.mp3"},{"sentence":"I see they’re advertising for a new Sales Director.","translation":"من می بینم که آنها برای یک مدیر فروش جدید تبلیغ می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000793569.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1bcc5f29-5c00-52b9-a871-d0011fb67780','8c28c71b-f03d-5a57-b915-6c94f4486a42',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'advertise the fact (that)','تبلیغ کردن (کالا، خدمت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5347da55-f3c4-51f5-b169-2d49c6489b6c','9c0c45f2-8955-5729-90a1-fad6f95d23ca',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the part of the day after the morning and before the evening',null,null,'بعدازظهر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Monday/Friday/Saturday etc afternoon Did you see the football on Saturday afternoon?','this afternoon (= today in the afternoon ) I''ll come round to your house this afternoon.','early/late afternoon I arrived in Boston in the early afternoon.','all afternoon/the whole afternoon You left the lights on all afternoon.','tomorrow afternoon What are you doing tomorrow afternoon?','yesterday afternoon I went to see mum yesterday afternoon.','an afternoon nap (= short sleep ) Dad was having his Sunday afternoon nap.','the afternoon sun It was too hot to go out in the afternoon sun.','afternoon tea (= a light meal eaten in the afternoon with a cup of tea ) Some people still have afternoon tea at 4 o''clock.','the middle of the afternoon It was the middle of a long hot summer afternoon.','spend the afternoon somewhere/doing something We decided to spend the afternoon in town.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There’s a meeting on Thursday afternoon .","translation":"بعد از ظهر پنجشنبه جلسه ای هست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650350.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was very hot in the afternoon .","translation":"بعد از ظهر خیلی گرم بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000975936.mp3"},{"sentence":"See you tomorrow afternoon .","translation":"فردا بعدازظهر میبینمت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650356.mp3"},{"sentence":"Are you going into town this afternoon ?","translation":"امروز بعدازظهر میری شهر؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000975937.mp3"},{"sentence":"We met in the early afternoon .","translation":"اوایل بعد از ظهر همدیگر را دیدیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941352.mp3"},{"sentence":"By late afternoon , Micky had changed his mind.","translation":"اواخر بعد از ظهر، میکی نظرش را تغییر داده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001913123.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was having his afternoon nap .","translation":"او داشت چرت بعدازظهر خود را می زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000975938.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('da28e6a1-fcfb-5230-b2dd-344382ecef71','9c0c45f2-8955-5729-90a1-fad6f95d23ca',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'afternoons','بعدازظهر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Monday/Friday/Saturday etc afternoon Did you see the football on Saturday afternoon?','this afternoon (= today in the afternoon ) I''ll come round to your house this afternoon.','early/late afternoon I arrived in Boston in the early afternoon.','all afternoon/the whole afternoon You left the lights on all afternoon.','tomorrow afternoon What are you doing tomorrow afternoon?','yesterday afternoon I went to see mum yesterday afternoon.','an afternoon nap (= short sleep ) Dad was having his Sunday afternoon nap.','the afternoon sun It was too hot to go out in the afternoon sun.','afternoon tea (= a light meal eaten in the afternoon with a cup of tea ) Some people still have afternoon tea at 4 o''clock.','the middle of the afternoon It was the middle of a long hot summer afternoon.','spend the afternoon somewhere/doing something We decided to spend the afternoon in town.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('30196d16-81e2-5a6c-a9e5-5283825d2434','1fec0d5c-dfec-5624-85e0-7dc0532ce92f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to greet someone when you meet them in the afternoon',null,null,'وقتی بعد از ظهر با کسی ملاقات می کردی به او سلام می کرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('39d67c86-003c-53f9-97cf-6409da310607','97cff517-2a1f-57ae-9b3e-10fde9dfdf71',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an arrangement or promise to do something, made by two or more people, companies, organizations etc','[ countable ]',null,'توافق، قرارداد، هم‌رأیی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an agreement We made an agreement not to tell anyone.','sign an agreement The two countries have signed an agreement on military co-operation.','have an agreement They have an agreement that all workers should be union members.','reach/come to an agreement ( also conclude an agreement formal ) It took the two sides several weeks to reach an agreement. The two sides failed to come to an agreement.','break/violate an agreement The UN accused the country''s leaders of breaking international agreements.','keep/honour an agreement ( also stick to an agreement informal ) (= do what you have agreed ) It’s important to keep to your student loan agreement.','go back on an agreement ( also renege on an agreement formal ) (= not do what you agreed to do ) Republican leaders accused Democrats of trying to renege on an agreement to have a House vote.','be bound by an agreement (= have to obey the conditions of an official agreement ) India is bound by the agreements signed under the World Trade Organisation.','negotiate an agreement (= discuss particular things in order to reach an agreement ) They have been trying to negotiate an agreement with a Chinese company.','hammer out an agreement informal (= decide on an agreement after a lot of discussion and disagreement ) Traders are focused on Washington, where Republicans and Democrats are hammering out an agreement to balance the federal budget.','draft an agreement (= write the conditions of an agreement, which may be changed ) The legal team will draft a second agreement incorporating these changes.','broker an agreement (= arrange an agreement between two or more opposing groups ) The US has been trying to broker an agreement between the Israelis and the Palestinians.','enter into an agreement formal (= make an official agreement, which has legal responsibilities ) In 2006 the city authorities entered into an agreement with a private firm to operate the gardens.','finalize an agreement (= agree the last part ) The developer hopes to finalise an agreement this week with the local authority.','an agreement breaks down (= it stops working )','a written agreement There is usually a written agreement between the borrower and the bank.','a verbal agreement (= agreed in words, but not written down ) The doctor needs to have a verbal agreement from the patient.','a trade agreement The administration has signed a multi-billion dollar trade agreement with Colombia.','a legal agreement The golf club is also offering to enter into a legal agreement with local residents.','a binding agreement (= an official agreement that must be obeyed ) Lawyers are in the process of drafting a legally binding agreement between both parties.','a formal/informal agreement','a peace agreement (= a permanent agreement to stop fighting ) The five countries in the region signed a peace agreement.','a ceasefire agreement (= a temporary agreement to stop fighting ) A ceasefire agreement was signed between the government and the rebels.','an international agreement an international agreement on combating climate change','a multilateral agreement formal (= involving several countries or groups ) a multilateral nuclear arms agreement','a bilateral agreement formal (= between two countries or groups ) a bilateral agreement between the UK and Korean governments','a draft agreement (= one that is not yet in its finished form ) The government of Iraq refused to accept the wording of the draft UN agreement.','a gentleman’s agreement (= an agreement that is not written down, and is based only on trust ) The candidates seemed to have a gentleman’s agreement not to criticize each other.','the terms of an agreement (= the conditions that people agree on ) Under the terms of the agreement, the debt would be repaid over a 20-year period.','a breach of an agreement (= an act of breaking an agreement ) Both sides were accusing each other of breaches of the agreement.','be close to an agreement (= have almost reached an agreement ) Management and unions are close to an agreement about pay.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They had made an agreement that they would share the profits equally.","translation":"آنها توافق کرده بودند که سود را به طور مساوی تقسیم کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000046.mp3"},{"sentence":"Haydon came to an agreement with his creditors.","translation":"هایدون با طلبکارانش به توافق رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662604.mp3"},{"sentence":"an agreement on arms reduction","translation":"توافق کاهش تسلیحات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000795463.mp3"},{"sentence":"Under the agreement, most agricultural prices will remain at the same level.","translation":"بر اساس این توافق، قیمت بیشتر محصولات کشاورزی در همان سطح باقی خواهد ماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000047.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('a12e3675-36c6-5984-8510-480734bb5c68','97cff517-2a1f-57ae-9b3e-10fde9dfdf71',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when people have the same opinion as each other','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی مردم نظری مشابه یکدیگر دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an agreement We made an agreement not to tell anyone.','sign an agreement The two countries have signed an agreement on military co-operation.','have an agreement They have an agreement that all workers should be union members.','reach/come to an agreement ( also conclude an agreement formal ) It took the two sides several weeks to reach an agreement. The two sides failed to come to an agreement.','break/violate an agreement The UN accused the country''s leaders of breaking international agreements.','keep/honour an agreement ( also stick to an agreement informal ) (= do what you have agreed ) It’s important to keep to your student loan agreement.','go back on an agreement ( also renege on an agreement formal ) (= not do what you agreed to do ) Republican leaders accused Democrats of trying to renege on an agreement to have a House vote.','be bound by an agreement (= have to obey the conditions of an official agreement ) India is bound by the agreements signed under the World Trade Organisation.','negotiate an agreement (= discuss particular things in order to reach an agreement ) They have been trying to negotiate an agreement with a Chinese company.','hammer out an agreement informal (= decide on an agreement after a lot of discussion and disagreement ) Traders are focused on Washington, where Republicans and Democrats are hammering out an agreement to balance the federal budget.','draft an agreement (= write the conditions of an agreement, which may be changed ) The legal team will draft a second agreement incorporating these changes.','broker an agreement (= arrange an agreement between two or more opposing groups ) The US has been trying to broker an agreement between the Israelis and the Palestinians.','enter into an agreement formal (= make an official agreement, which has legal responsibilities ) In 2006 the city authorities entered into an agreement with a private firm to operate the gardens.','finalize an agreement (= agree the last part ) The developer hopes to finalise an agreement this week with the local authority.','an agreement breaks down (= it stops working )','a written agreement There is usually a written agreement between the borrower and the bank.','a verbal agreement (= agreed in words, but not written down ) The doctor needs to have a verbal agreement from the patient.','a trade agreement The administration has signed a multi-billion dollar trade agreement with Colombia.','a legal agreement The golf club is also offering to enter into a legal agreement with local residents.','a binding agreement (= an official agreement that must be obeyed ) Lawyers are in the process of drafting a legally binding agreement between both parties.','a formal/informal agreement','a peace agreement (= a permanent agreement to stop fighting ) The five countries in the region signed a peace agreement.','a ceasefire agreement (= a temporary agreement to stop fighting ) A ceasefire agreement was signed between the government and the rebels.','an international agreement an international agreement on combating climate change','a multilateral agreement formal (= involving several countries or groups ) a multilateral nuclear arms agreement','a bilateral agreement formal (= between two countries or groups ) a bilateral agreement between the UK and Korean governments','a draft agreement (= one that is not yet in its finished form ) The government of Iraq refused to accept the wording of the draft UN agreement.','a gentleman’s agreement (= an agreement that is not written down, and is based only on trust ) The candidates seemed to have a gentleman’s agreement not to criticize each other.','the terms of an agreement (= the conditions that people agree on ) Under the terms of the agreement, the debt would be repaid over a 20-year period.','a breach of an agreement (= an act of breaking an agreement ) Both sides were accusing each other of breaches of the agreement.','be close to an agreement (= have almost reached an agreement ) Management and unions are close to an agreement about pay.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is general agreement that copyright is a good idea.","translation":"توافق کلی وجود دارد که کپی رایت ایده خوبی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000795479.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is widespread agreement on the need for prison reform.","translation":"توافق گسترده ای در مورد نیاز به اصلاح زندان وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000795482.mp3"},{"sentence":"A decision will not be made until everyone is in agreement.","translation":"تا زمانی که همه موافق نباشند تصمیمی گرفته نمی شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000795485.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is easier for two parties to reach agreement than for three.","translation":"رسیدن به توافق برای دو طرف آسانتر از سه طرف است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001662617.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
