('c882b7bc-b98b-5b43-ad1e-d0bf77c41e6c','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'conditions','حالت، وضعیت؛ شرط؛ بیماری؛ (شرایط) شرایط','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8fbe5ce2-9b36-5415-af17-f83d8a402796','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',4,'state','دولت','spoken & written','the state that something is in, especially how good or bad its physical state is','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'حالتی که چیزی در آن قرار دارد، به خصوص اینکه وضعیت فیزیکی آن چقدر خوب یا بد است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The car has been well maintained and is in excellent condition.","translation":"ماشین به خوبی نگهداری شده و در شرایط عالی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100693.mp3"},{"sentence":"The house was in a terrible condition.","translation":"خانه در وضعیت وحشتناکی قرار داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717111.mp3"},{"sentence":"The condition of nuclear plants is a matter of great concern.","translation":"وضعیت نیروگاه های هسته ای یک موضوع بسیار نگران کننده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100690.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1dfff415-e876-586f-adfb-03abed856201','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',5,'health/fitness','سلامت / تناسب اندام','spoken & written','how healthy or fit you are','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'چقدر سالم یا تناسب اندام هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She is being treated at Walton Hospital, where her condition is described as ‘satisfactory’.","translation":"او در بیمارستان والتون تحت درمان است، جایی که وضعیت او \"رضایت بخش\" توصیف شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100774.mp3"},{"sentence":"One of the victims was in a critical condition after suffering severe burns.","translation":"یکی از قربانیان پس از سوختگی شدید در وضعیت وخیمی قرار داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717115.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you are uncertain about your physical condition, check with your doctor before trying these exercises.","translation":"اگر در مورد وضعیت بدنی خود مطمئن نیستید، قبل از انجام این تمرینات با پزشک خود مشورت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717118.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘I’m so out of condition (= unfit ) , ’ she panted.","translation":"او نفس نفس می زد: «من خیلی بی شرایطم (= نامناسب).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100778.mp3"},{"sentence":"an athlete in peak condition","translation":"یک ورزشکار در اوج شرایط","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717123.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was in no condition to cope with a train journey.","translation":"من در شرایطی نبودم که بتوانم با یک سفر قطار کنار بیایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100782.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mark can’t possibly drive home in that condition (= when he is so drunk, ill, or upset ) .","translation":"مارک احتمالاً نمی تواند در آن شرایط (= وقتی خیلی مست، مریض یا ناراحت است) به خانه برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717126.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('eb8e3847-a586-535f-950e-41d5f04b800b','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',6,'agreement/contract','توافق / قرارداد','spoken & written','something that you must agree to in order for something to happen, especially when this is included in a contract','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که شما باید با آن موافقت کنید تا اتفاقی بیفتد، به خصوص زمانی که در قرارداد گنجانده شده باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['lay down/set/impose conditions (= say what someone must agree to ) They laid down certain conditions before agreeing to the ceasefire.','attach a condition (= say that an agreement depends on something ) Only one condition was attached to this agreement.','accept/agree to conditions He refused to accept the conditions set by the rebel leader.','meet/satisfy/fulfil a condition (= do what has been agreed ) In order to get a state pension, you must satisfy certain conditions.','comply with/observe a condition (= act according to a condition ) You must agree to comply with the bank’s conditions before you can get a loan.','a strict condition The US agreed to give financial aid, with a number of strict conditions.','on condition that formal (= only if a particular thing is agreed to ) The police released him on condition that he return the following week.','on one condition (= only if one particular thing is agreed to ) You can go, but only on one condition - you have to be back by eleven.','on certain conditions He said we could rent the house from him on certain conditions.','terms and conditions (= what a contract says must be done ) Before you buy online, make sure you read the terms and conditions.','be subject to a condition (= depend on a particular thing that must be done ) Permission to build on the land will be subject to certain conditions.','a breach of (a) condition (= an act of not doing what has been agreed ) You can sue the company for a breach of condition.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She laid down only one condition : that her name not be revealed.","translation":"او فقط یک شرط گذاشت: نامش فاش نشود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939808.mp3"},{"sentence":"There were strict conditions for letting us use their information.","translation":"شرایط سختی وجود داشت که به ما اجازه می داد از اطلاعات آنها استفاده کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100732.mp3"},{"sentence":"The bank agreed to extend the loan if certain conditions were met .","translation":"بانک با تمدید وام در صورت رعایت شرایط خاص موافقت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939814.mp3"},{"sentence":"A statement of your terms and conditions of employment can be found in the Personnel Handbook.","translation":"بیانیه شرایط و ضوابط استخدام شما را می توان در کتابچه راهنمای پرسنل یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717132.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was released on bail on condition that he did not go within half a mile of his mother’s address.","translation":"او به شرط وثیقه آزاد شد که تا نیم مایلی آدرس مادرش نرود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939820.mp3"},{"sentence":"The application was approved, subject to certain conditions .","translation":"این برنامه با شرایط خاصی تأیید شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717140.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('9eb0e363-9920-5180-905a-89e9b66aaa0c','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',7,'for something to happen','برای اینکه اتفاقی بیفتد','spoken & written','something that must exist or happen first, before something else can happen','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که باید وجود داشته باشد یا ابتدا اتفاق بیفتد، قبل از اینکه اتفاق دیگری رخ دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Our goal is to create the conditions for a lasting peace.","translation":"هدف ما ایجاد شرایط برای صلح پایدار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717148.mp3"},{"sentence":"Investment is a necessary condition of economic growth.","translation":"سرمایه گذاری شرط لازم رشد اقتصادی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717149.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bac7c404-28cd-51a9-8f08-d326a25336a6','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',8,'illness','بیماری','spoken & written','an illness or health problem that affects you permanently or for a very long time','[ countable ]',null,'یک بیماری یا مشکل سلامتی که شما را برای همیشه یا برای مدت طولانی تحت تاثیر قرار می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"People suffering from this condition should not smoke.","translation":"افرادی که از این عارضه رنج می برند نباید سیگار بکشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100764.mp3"},{"sentence":"She has a serious heart condition.","translation":"او یک بیماری قلبی جدی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100767.mp3"},{"sentence":"Was he being treated for any medical condition ?","translation":"آیا او به دلیل شرایط پزشکی تحت درمان بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717159.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ebf93c90-2a48-512e-bee8-37d0c39143ca','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',9,'situation of group','وضعیت گروه','formal','the situation or state of a particular group of people, especially when they have problems and difficulties','[ singular ]',null,'وضعیت یا وضعیت یک گروه خاص از مردم، به ویژه زمانی که آنها مشکلات و مشکلاتی دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the condition of the poor in our cities","translation":"وضعیت فقرا در شهرهای ما","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100794.mp3"},{"sentence":"All my paintings are ultimately about the human condition .","translation":"تمام نقاشی های من در نهایت در مورد وضعیت انسان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717165.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('92acf151-e162-502b-bedf-d65a5e2afda8','f007c2e4-a0d8-5bff-a932-2764ab7b0c4b',10,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'on no condition','حالت، وضعیت؛ شرط؛ بیماری؛ (شرایط) شرایط','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6864a90a-b843-5382-bbb0-5c8115f7f94f','9a9f4940-aa42-5c56-8df5-0db1fa3c8b56',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make a person or an animal think or behave in a certain way by influencing or training them over a period of time','[ transitive ]',null,'وادار کردن شخص یا حیوانی به روشی خاص با تأثیرگذاری یا آموزش آنها در یک دوره زمانی خاص فکر کند یا رفتار کند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"People are conditioned by society.","translation":"مردم مشروط به جامعه هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100804.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many women are conditioned from birth to be accepting rather than questioning.","translation":"بسیاری از زنان از بدو تولد مشروط به پذیرفتن به جای سوال کردن هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717180.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c06c17a4-b155-5956-85b1-c310eb1d92cc','9a9f4940-aa42-5c56-8df5-0db1fa3c8b56',2,null,null,'formal','to control or decide the way in which something can happen or exist','[ transitive ]',null,'برای کنترل یا تصمیم گیری در مورد راهی که در آن چیزی می تواند اتفاق بیفتد یا وجود داشته باشد',array['determine']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"What I buy is conditioned by the amount I earn.","translation":"چیزی که من میخرم مشروط به میزان درآمد من است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100817.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f95c7ee8-92df-5ee1-860d-726a45c4fe16','9a9f4940-aa42-5c56-8df5-0db1fa3c8b56',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to keep hair or skin healthy by putting a special liquid on it','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای حفظ سلامت مو یا پوست با قرار دادن مایع مخصوص روی آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a shampoo that washes and conditions all in one","translation":"شامپویی که همه را در یک واحد شستشو و حالت می دهد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001100821.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5631b850-d60d-5689-bbb4-8db12807c2fa','1f89b782-bec3-507d-b1f3-21c3c43b62de',1,null,null,'spoken & written','sure that something will happen in the way that you want or expect','[ not before noun ]',null,'مطمئن، واثق؛ خودباور','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We are confident next year’s profits will be higher.","translation":"ما مطمئن هستیم که سود سال آینده بیشتر خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716913.mp3"},{"sentence":"He is quietly confident that there will be no problems this time.","translation":"او بی سر و صدا مطمئن است که این بار هیچ مشکلی وجود نخواهد داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716914.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Prime Minister appeared relaxed and confident of winning an overall majority.","translation":"نخست وزیر آرام به نظر می رسید و از کسب اکثریت کلی مطمئن بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716920.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company is confident of success .","translation":"این شرکت به موفقیت خود اطمینان دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716924.mp3"},{"sentence":"I feel quite confident about the future.","translation":"من نسبت به آینده کاملاً مطمئن هستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716930.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('3847c8a5-8728-5d1b-a3ae-403aa8e3934e','1f89b782-bec3-507d-b1f3-21c3c43b62de',2,null,null,'spoken & written','sure that you have the ability to do things well or deal with situations successfully',null,null,'مطمئن باشید که توانایی انجام کارها را به خوبی یا کنار آمدن با موقعیت ها با موفقیت دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Despite her disability, Philippa is very confident.","translation":"فیلیپا علیرغم معلولیت خود بسیار مطمئن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716936.mp3"},{"sentence":"I feel much more confident about myself and my abilities these days.","translation":"این روزها نسبت به خودم و توانایی هایم خیلی بیشتر احساس اطمینان می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716939.mp3"},{"sentence":"He began to read in a calm confident voice.","translation":"با صدایی آرام و مطمئن شروع به خواندن کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000853391.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('261d2b10-12af-5aae-9b13-b7d28e137e04','1f89b782-bec3-507d-b1f3-21c3c43b62de',3,null,null,'spoken & written','sure that something is true',null,null,'مطمئن باشید که چیزی درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We are confident we have done nothing wrong.","translation":"ما مطمئن هستیم که هیچ اشتباهی انجام نداده ایم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716954.mp3"},{"sentence":"He began to feel confident that Zaborski was only guessing.","translation":"او شروع به احساس اطمینان کرد که زابورسکی فقط حدس می‌زند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716955.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is not possible to give a confident answer to the question of whether the delay was unreasonable.","translation":"نمی توان به این سوال که آیا تاخیر غیرمنطقی بوده است، پاسخ مطمئنی داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000355.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1617e809-3360-5671-971e-14f1154e0120','c750c558-b01f-588f-8efb-882c0342dcb2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','unclear and difficult to understand',null,null,'گیج‌کننده، سردرگم‌کننده','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The instructions were really confusing.","translation":"دستورالعمل ها واقعا گیج کننده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854911.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was a very confusing situation.","translation":"وضعیت بسیار گیج کننده ای بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854912.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('63df4126-2820-543e-af67-f83e7d30b11b','e0c610c4-a318-54c0-a1c8-90d2575fb63d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','when you do not understand what is happening or what something means because it is not clear','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'سردرگمی، آشفتگی؛ آشوب؛ اشتباه گرفتن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/create confusion English spelling often causes confusion for learners.','lead to/result in confusion The differing instructions led to confusion.','add to the confusion (= make something more confusing ) There were a lot of rumours, which added to the confusion.','throw/plunge somebody into confusion The unexpected news threw us all into confusion.','clear up the confusion (= explain something more clearly ) The chairman said that he would try to clear up the confusion.','confusion arises (= begins ) The confusion arose because of a complete misunderstanding.','great confusion We looked at each other in great confusion.','complete/total/utter confusion Candy''s eyes showed her total confusion.','considerable confusion The movie jumps backwards and forwards in time, which causes considerable confusion.','general confusion There was general confusion about the effects of the new law.','mental confusion Mental confusion is one of the symptoms of the disease.','a state of confusion People were in a state of confusion and close to panic.','(in order) to avoid confusion Doctors should explain their instructions to patients carefully, to avoid any confusion.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was some confusion as to whether we had won or lost.","translation":"در مورد اینکه ما بردیم یا باختیم سردرگمی وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854930.mp3"},{"sentence":"The diversion led to considerable confusion .","translation":"انحراف منجر به سردرگمی قابل توجهی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854933.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9e8ec199-e149-57b7-b4d3-542092a3317a','e0c610c4-a318-54c0-a1c8-90d2575fb63d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which someone wrongly thinks that a person or thing is someone or something else','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن کسی به اشتباه فکر می کند که یک شخص یا چیز، شخص یا چیز دیگری است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/create confusion English spelling often causes confusion for learners.','lead to/result in confusion The differing instructions led to confusion.','add to the confusion (= make something more confusing ) There were a lot of rumours, which added to the confusion.','throw/plunge somebody into confusion The unexpected news threw us all into confusion.','clear up the confusion (= explain something more clearly ) The chairman said that he would try to clear up the confusion.','confusion arises (= begins ) The confusion arose because of a complete misunderstanding.','great confusion We looked at each other in great confusion.','complete/total/utter confusion Candy''s eyes showed her total confusion.','considerable confusion The movie jumps backwards and forwards in time, which causes considerable confusion.','general confusion There was general confusion about the effects of the new law.','mental confusion Mental confusion is one of the symptoms of the disease.','a state of confusion People were in a state of confusion and close to panic.','(in order) to avoid confusion Doctors should explain their instructions to patients carefully, to avoid any confusion.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"To avoid confusion, the teams wore different colours.","translation":"برای جلوگیری از سردرگمی، تیم‌ها رنگ‌های مختلف پوشیدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854937.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is a confusion in the public mind between psychology and psychiatry.","translation":"در اذهان عمومی بین روانشناسی و روانپزشکی سردرگمی وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854940.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('738a1340-c7dc-58e5-b09e-5c3979975a0f','e0c610c4-a318-54c0-a1c8-90d2575fb63d',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling of not being able to think clearly about what you should say or do, especially in an embarrassing situation','[ uncountable ]',null,'احساس ناتوانی در فکر کردن واضح در مورد آنچه باید بگویید یا انجام دهید، به خصوص در یک موقعیت شرم آور','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/create confusion English spelling often causes confusion for learners.','lead to/result in confusion The differing instructions led to confusion.','add to the confusion (= make something more confusing ) There were a lot of rumours, which added to the confusion.','throw/plunge somebody into confusion The unexpected news threw us all into confusion.','clear up the confusion (= explain something more clearly ) The chairman said that he would try to clear up the confusion.','confusion arises (= begins ) The confusion arose because of a complete misunderstanding.','great confusion We looked at each other in great confusion.','complete/total/utter confusion Candy''s eyes showed her total confusion.','considerable confusion The movie jumps backwards and forwards in time, which causes considerable confusion.','general confusion There was general confusion about the effects of the new law.','mental confusion Mental confusion is one of the symptoms of the disease.','a state of confusion People were in a state of confusion and close to panic.','(in order) to avoid confusion Doctors should explain their instructions to patients carefully, to avoid any confusion.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"His confusion at meeting her there was quite apparent.","translation":"سردرگمی او در ملاقات با او در آنجا کاملاً آشکار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854944.mp3"},{"sentence":"Matt stared at her in confusion.","translation":"مت گیج به او خیره شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703411.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('5c433a95-6107-53ef-a998-332a34b234ed','e0c610c4-a318-54c0-a1c8-90d2575fb63d',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a very confusing situation, that usually has a lot of noise and action, so that it is difficult for someone to understand it or control it','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک موقعیت بسیار گیج کننده، که معمولاً سر و صدا و کنش زیادی دارد، به طوری که درک یا کنترل آن برای کسی دشوار است.',array['chaos']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['cause/create confusion English spelling often causes confusion for learners.','lead to/result in confusion The differing instructions led to confusion.','add to the confusion (= make something more confusing ) There were a lot of rumours, which added to the confusion.','throw/plunge somebody into confusion The unexpected news threw us all into confusion.','clear up the confusion (= explain something more clearly ) The chairman said that he would try to clear up the confusion.','confusion arises (= begins ) The confusion arose because of a complete misunderstanding.','great confusion We looked at each other in great confusion.','complete/total/utter confusion Candy''s eyes showed her total confusion.','considerable confusion The movie jumps backwards and forwards in time, which causes considerable confusion.','general confusion There was general confusion about the effects of the new law.','mental confusion Mental confusion is one of the symptoms of the disease.','a state of confusion People were in a state of confusion and close to panic.','(in order) to avoid confusion Doctors should explain their instructions to patients carefully, to avoid any confusion.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a scene of indescribable confusion","translation":"صحنه ای از سردرگمی وصف ناپذیر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854951.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a confusion of shouts and orders as the ship prepared to depart.","translation":"در حالی که کشتی آماده حرکت می شد، سردرگمی از فریادها و دستورات به وجود آمد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703413.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('f2a97c79-e84e-58cd-b346-912a4d5b8f1a','50d0d47e-df40-56a1-b6ed-d7c1d995d229',1,'aware','آگاه است','spoken & written','noticing or realizing something','[ not before noun ]',null,'آگاه، بیدار؛ عمدی و آگاهانه',array['aware']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I became conscious of someone watching me.","translation":"حواسم به این بود که کسی مرا تماشا می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675175.mp3"},{"sentence":"I was very conscious of the fact that I had to make a good impression.","translation":"من از این واقعیت آگاه بودم که باید تأثیر خوبی بگذارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000855813.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was conscious that Marie was listening to every word.","translation":"او آگاه بود که ماری به تک تک کلمات گوش می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000855816.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4bdafcae-d159-5286-b5e6-766a40ae2dc0','50d0d47e-df40-56a1-b6ed-d7c1d995d229',2,'awake','بیدار','spoken & written','awake and able to understand what is happening around you',null,null,'بیدار و قادر به درک آنچه در اطراف شما اتفاق می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The driver was still conscious when the ambulance arrived.","translation":"وقتی آمبولانس رسید راننده هنوز هوشیار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000855821.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('543b2ee9-149d-5a68-81a8-bd649673ce18','50d0d47e-df40-56a1-b6ed-d7c1d995d229',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'conscious effort/decision/attempt etc','آگاه، بیدار؛ عمدی و آگاهانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('2496df44-5279-5a31-a052-bf97c712df95','50d0d47e-df40-56a1-b6ed-d7c1d995d229',4,'concerned','نگران است','spoken & written','thinking a lot about or concerned about something',null,'self-conscious','زیاد فکر کردن یا نگرانی در مورد چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['socially/politically/environmentally etc conscious (= conscious of social/political etc issues ) We have all become more environmentally conscious.','health conscious People are health conscious nowadays and careful about what they eat.','fashion conscious Young girls are always very fashion conscious.','security conscious Most airports are extremely security conscious.','safety conscious Workers are encouraged to be safety conscious.','cost conscious Companies keen to increase their profits have to be cost conscious.','class conscious (= concerned about what class of society people come from ) In the past, people were much more class conscious.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"environmentally conscious consumers","translation":"مصرف کنندگان آگاه به محیط زیست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675187.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many employers are becoming more safety-conscious.","translation":"بسیاری از کارفرمایان به ایمنی بیشتر توجه می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675190.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was very conscious of security.","translation":"او از امنیت بسیار آگاه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675193.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('558809a6-f77f-5d20-87d7-c1a346641665','50d0d47e-df40-56a1-b6ed-d7c1d995d229',5,'thoughts','افکار','spoken & written','conscious thoughts , memories etc are ones which you know about',null,null,'افکار آگاهانه، خاطرات و غیره آنهایی هستند که شما در مورد آنها می دانید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the conscious mind","translation":"ذهن خودآگاه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675201.mp3"},{"sentence":"Without conscious thought, she instinctively placed a hand on his arm.","translation":"بدون فکر آگاهانه، به طور غریزی دستی را روی بازوی او گذاشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675202.mp3"},{"sentence":"It affects the audience at a deeper, less conscious level.","translation":"در سطحی عمیق تر و کمتر آگاهانه بر مخاطب تأثیر می گذارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675203.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b6b240d5-be1d-5a34-b028-22c27378e2be','5fe87240-3a92-5e99-927c-e9878551acbc',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to build something such as a house, bridge , road etc',null,null,'ساختن، بنا کردن (به‌نحو فنی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are plans to construct a new road bridge across the river.","translation":"برنامه‌هایی برای ساخت یک پل جاده‌ای جدید بر روی رودخانه وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001106033.mp3"},{"sentence":"skyscrapers constructed entirely of concrete and glass","translation":"آسمان خراش هایی که تماماً از بتن و شیشه ساخته شده اند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001106036.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('cfb16cf4-b375-59d8-a53a-0d78cbdd7c7f','5fe87240-3a92-5e99-927c-e9878551acbc',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to form something such as a sentence , argument , or system by joining words, ideas etc together',null,null,'برای تشکیل چیزی مانند یک جمله، استدلال یا سیستم با به هم پیوستن کلمات، ایده ها و غیره به یکدیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Boyce has constructed a new theory of management.","translation":"بویس تئوری جدیدی از مدیریت ساخته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001106040.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('dc186972-59d7-52d2-938f-02dfee85bc2f','5fe87240-3a92-5e99-927c-e9878551acbc',3,null,null,'technical','to draw a mathematical shape',null,null,'برای رسم یک شکل ریاضی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Construct a square with sides of 5 cm.","translation":"یک مربع با اضلاع 5 سانتی متر بسازید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001106046.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('024a3d9e-4b2e-5790-aeaf-4da419558275','ea44298a-5ecc-5cbf-a686-d9ff0d2b58b3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an idea formed by combining several pieces of information or knowledge',null,null,'ایده ای که از ترکیب چند قطعه اطلاعات یا دانش شکل می گیرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b715be78-d653-530c-a2ef-21ee68ec0c0d','ea44298a-5ecc-5cbf-a686-d9ff0d2b58b3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is built or made',null,null,'چیزی که ساخته یا ساخته شده است',array['construction']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8e2ac02b-b03a-547a-84f6-c02422a295b0','59317364-476b-5c07-8384-04be48148f0f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a standard that you use to judge something or make a decision about something',null,null,'معیار، ملاک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['meet/satisfy/fulfil the criteria Does your experience meet the criteria for the job?','use criteria What criteria do we use to decide whether one book is better than another?','apply criteria (= use them ) There are certain criteria you should apply when buying a computer.','be based on criteria Normal child development is based upon certain criteria.','establish the criteria for something Management establishes the criteria for each project.','the main criterion You need to decide on your main criteria before you buy a house.','the sole criterion (= the only one ) Examination results are still seen as the sole criterion of success in education.','a strict criterion (= very exact ) All the cars must meet strict criteria, and are tested by our mechanics.','academic/political/environmental etc criteria The winning product must satisfy a range of environmental criteria.','an objective criterion (= that is based on fact and not opinion ) The label of ''carer'' was defined by the objective criterion of someone who spends more than seven hours looking after someone.','a set of criteria Doctors use an established set of criteria for making a diagnosis.','a list of criteria There’s a list of criteria that you must meet in order to pass your driving test.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the criteria we use to select candidates","translation":"معیارهایی که برای انتخاب نامزدها استفاده می کنیم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846837.mp3"},{"sentence":"the criteria for measuring how good schools are","translation":"معیارهای سنجش میزان خوب بودن مدارس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846840.mp3"},{"sentence":"Academic ability is not the sole criterion for admission to the college.","translation":"توانایی تحصیلی تنها ملاک پذیرش در کالج نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000401.mp3"},{"sentence":"a universal set of criteria for diagnosing patients","translation":"مجموعه ای جهانی از معیارها برای تشخیص بیماران","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756103.mp3"},{"sentence":"To qualify for a grant, students must satisfy certain criteria.","translation":"برای واجد شرایط بودن برای کمک هزینه، دانش آموزان باید معیارهای خاصی را رعایت کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756109.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('24885b95-8ba0-5980-bfc3-90903a8046b8','6ae73dc5-58ea-54a1-9a77-5dc4f49047f5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','remarks that say what you think is bad about someone or something',null,null,'نکوهش، نقد؛ انتقاد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong/severe/heavy criticism This decision attracted heavy criticism from environmental groups.','fierce/bitter/harsh/sharp criticism (= involving angry feelings ) The prison system has been the object of fierce criticism.','public criticism As a politician, you have to get used to public criticism.','constructive criticism (= aimed at improving something or someone in a helpful way ) Praise and constructive criticism are both very useful.','widespread criticism There was widespread criticism of his speech.','growing/mounting criticism The government was faced with mounting criticism at home and abroad.','outspoken criticism (= said very openly and directly ) I was surprised by his outspoken criticism of the system.','implied criticism (= suggested indirectly, rather than said openly ) She sensed the implied criticism in his remarks.','draw/attract/provoke criticism (= be criticized ) The plan has drawn criticism from some groups.','come under criticism/come in for criticism (= be criticized ) The deal came under fierce criticism from other American airlines.','meet (with) criticism (= be criticized ) His theory met with harsh criticism from colleagues.','face criticism He has often faced criticism in the local press.','accept/take criticism (= allow it and learn from it ) Very few people know how to accept criticism.','level criticism at somebody/something (= aim it at someone or something ) A great deal of criticism was levelled at the company.','single somebody out for criticism (= to criticize one person, organization etc specifically ) The goalkeeper was singled out for criticism.','be the subject of criticism/be subjected to criticism (= be criticized by people ) The club has been the subject of criticism since last October.','be open to criticism (= be willing or able to accept it ) Management have decided this and I don''t think they''re open to criticism.','be sensitive to criticism (= to react to criticism, often in a bad way ) He was highly sensitive to criticism in the press.','a storm/barrage of criticism (= a lot of criticism ) His comments provoked a barrage of criticism.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"My main criticism of the scheme is that it does nothing to help families on low incomes.","translation":"انتقاد اصلی من از این طرح این است که هیچ کمکی به خانواده های کم درآمد نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756158.mp3"},{"sentence":"Despite strong criticism , the new system is still in place.","translation":"علیرغم انتقادهای شدید، سیستم جدید هنوز پابرجاست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756163.mp3"},{"sentence":"There has been widespread criticism of the decision.","translation":"انتقادات گسترده ای از این تصمیم وجود داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756159.mp3"},{"sentence":"We try to give students constructive criticism .","translation":"ما سعی می کنیم به دانش آموزان انتقاد سازنده داشته باشیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756167.mp3"},{"sentence":"Another criticism levelled at him was that his teaching methods were old-fashioned.","translation":"انتقاد دیگری که به او وارد شد این بود که روش های تدریس او قدیمی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756174.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government’s economic strategy has attracted a lot of criticism .","translation":"راهبرد اقتصادی دولت انتقادات زیادی را برانگیخته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756177.mp3"},{"sentence":"You must learn to accept criticism .","translation":"شما باید یاد بگیرید که انتقاد را بپذیرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939741.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many employees find it hard to take even mild criticism .","translation":"بسیاری از کارمندان تحمل انتقاد خفیف را برایشان سخت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939745.mp3"},{"sentence":"His actions provoked severe criticism from civil rights groups.","translation":"اقدامات او انتقاد شدید گروه های حقوق مدنی را برانگیخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845629.mp3"},{"sentence":"the storm of criticism that followed his announcement","translation":"طوفان انتقاداتی که پس از اعلام وی صورت گرفت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845635.mp3"}]'::jsonb,10),
('b29ff5bb-5f91-5833-8e5d-338bf4288b4a','6ae73dc5-58ea-54a1-9a77-5dc4f49047f5',2,null,null,'spoken & written','writing which expresses judgments about the good or bad qualities of books, films , music etc',null,null,'نوشته ای که قضاوت هایی را در مورد کیفیت خوب یا بد کتاب ها، فیلم ها، موسیقی و غیره بیان می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strong/severe/heavy criticism This decision attracted heavy criticism from environmental groups.','fierce/bitter/harsh/sharp criticism (= involving angry feelings ) The prison system has been the object of fierce criticism.','public criticism As a politician, you have to get used to public criticism.','constructive criticism (= aimed at improving something or someone in a helpful way ) Praise and constructive criticism are both very useful.','widespread criticism There was widespread criticism of his speech.','growing/mounting criticism The government was faced with mounting criticism at home and abroad.','outspoken criticism (= said very openly and directly ) I was surprised by his outspoken criticism of the system.','implied criticism (= suggested indirectly, rather than said openly ) She sensed the implied criticism in his remarks.','draw/attract/provoke criticism (= be criticized ) The plan has drawn criticism from some groups.','come under criticism/come in for criticism (= be criticized ) The deal came under fierce criticism from other American airlines.','meet (with) criticism (= be criticized ) His theory met with harsh criticism from colleagues.','face criticism He has often faced criticism in the local press.','accept/take criticism (= allow it and learn from it ) Very few people know how to accept criticism.','level criticism at somebody/something (= aim it at someone or something ) A great deal of criticism was levelled at the company.','single somebody out for criticism (= to criticize one person, organization etc specifically ) The goalkeeper was singled out for criticism.','be the subject of criticism/be subjected to criticism (= be criticized by people ) The club has been the subject of criticism since last October.','be open to criticism (= be willing or able to accept it ) Management have decided this and I don''t think they''re open to criticism.','be sensitive to criticism (= to react to criticism, often in a bad way ) He was highly sensitive to criticism in the press.','a storm/barrage of criticism (= a lot of criticism ) His comments provoked a barrage of criticism.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"literary criticism","translation":"نقد ادبی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001503322.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ad7242dc-f57d-5ab4-bf8c-340f00ec150d','649660c1-50dc-5452-83fe-86e90a2dd8b4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to express your disapproval of someone or something, or to talk about their faults','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'انتقاد کردن، نکوهش کردن؛ نقد کردن (اثر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strongly/severely/heavily criticize somebody/something Public transport has been severely criticized in the report.','sharply/harshly/fiercely criticize somebody/something (= in an angry way ) His attorney sharply criticized the police yesterday.','be widely criticized The proposal was widely criticized.','publicly criticize somebody/something The head coach publicly criticized the referee’s decision.','roundly criticize somebody/something (= strongly and severely ) Their research has been roundly criticized.','openly criticize somebody/something (= in a public and direct way ) They openly criticized the government’s handling of the crisis.','repeatedly/frequently/constantly criticize The fashion industry is frequently criticized for presenting extremely thin models as beautiful.','be quick to criticize somebody/something Some groups were quick to criticize the president.','criticize somebody/something on the grounds that (= for the reason that ) The survey was criticized on the grounds that the sample was too small.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Ron does nothing but criticize and complain all the time.","translation":"رون کاری جز انتقاد و شکایت مدام انجام نمی دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846956.mp3"},{"sentence":"The decision has been strongly criticized by teachers.","translation":"این تصمیم به شدت مورد انتقاد معلمان قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756184.mp3"},{"sentence":"The new law has been widely criticized .","translation":"قانون جدید انتقادات زیادی را به دنبال داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756185.mp3"},{"sentence":"He has been criticized for incompetence.","translation":"او به دلیل بی کفایتی مورد انتقاد قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756191.mp3"},{"sentence":"Doctors have criticized the government for failing to invest enough in the health service.","translation":"پزشکان از دولت انتقاد کرده اند که نتوانسته است به اندازه کافی در خدمات بهداشتی سرمایه گذاری کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756192.mp3"},{"sentence":"The report has been criticized as inaccurate and incomplete.","translation":"این گزارش به عنوان نادرست و ناقص مورد انتقاد قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001756195.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('e4264eb6-56f5-5562-9e6d-124e4d33a66d','649660c1-50dc-5452-83fe-86e90a2dd8b4',2,null,null,'formal','to express judgments about the good and bad qualities of something','[ transitive ]',null,'بیان قضاوت در مورد خصوصیات خوب و بد چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['strongly/severely/heavily criticize somebody/something Public transport has been severely criticized in the report.','sharply/harshly/fiercely criticize somebody/something (= in an angry way ) His attorney sharply criticized the police yesterday.','be widely criticized The proposal was widely criticized.','publicly criticize somebody/something The head coach publicly criticized the referee’s decision.','roundly criticize somebody/something (= strongly and severely ) Their research has been roundly criticized.','openly criticize somebody/something (= in a public and direct way ) They openly criticized the government’s handling of the crisis.','repeatedly/frequently/constantly criticize The fashion industry is frequently criticized for presenting extremely thin models as beautiful.','be quick to criticize somebody/something Some groups were quick to criticize the president.','criticize somebody/something on the grounds that (= for the reason that ) The survey was criticized on the grounds that the sample was too small.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We look at each other’s work and criticize it.","translation":"ما به کار یکدیگر نگاه می کنیم و از آن انتقاد می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000846964.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('72c081ca-e07e-5913-ab40-30b680a1a5a7','3f28cd67-e0bd-50d6-a389-1b0be8e4d1df',1,null,null,'spoken & written','at the present time',null,null,'در حال حاضر، فعلاً','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the products that are currently available","translation":"محصولاتی که در حال حاضر موجود هستند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000829046.mp3"},{"sentence":"He is currently working on his first novel.","translation":"او در حال حاضر مشغول کار بر روی اولین رمان خود است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000829045.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4908ae5f-972e-5d69-9b14-f421ec698443','9ee47b14-88af-5b45-abda-69e9ac2edab3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','able or likely to harm or kill you',null,null,'خطرناک، پرمخاطره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"laws about dangerous dogs","translation":"قوانین در مورد سگ های خطرناک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000832774.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some of these prisoners are extremely dangerous.","translation":"برخی از این زندانیان به شدت خطرناک هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001798955.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was a highly dangerous situation.","translation":"وضعیت بسیار خطرناکی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020051.mp3"},{"sentence":"The crumbling sidewalks are dangerous for old people.","translation":"فرو ریختن پیاده روها برای افراد مسن خطرناک است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001798960.mp3"},{"sentence":"The virus is probably not dangerous to humans.","translation":"این ویروس احتمالا برای انسان خطرناک نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001798963.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s dangerous for a woman to walk alone at night.","translation":"برای زن تنها راه رفتن در شب خطرناک است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000832778.mp3"},{"sentence":"The powdered milk was not as good as breast milk, and was downright dangerous (= actually dangerous ) when it was mixed with unclean water.","translation":"شیرخشک به خوبی شیر مادر نبود و وقتی با آب ناپاک مخلوط می شد کاملاً خطرناک بود (= در واقع خطرناک).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001798964.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('7c0c9b1a-3409-5e31-9e41-9de87db932a9','9ee47b14-88af-5b45-abda-69e9ac2edab3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','involving a lot of risk , or likely to cause problems',null,null,'مستلزم خطرات زیادی است یا احتمالاً باعث ایجاد مشکل می شود',array['risky']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The business is in a dangerous financial position.","translation":"کسب و کار در موقعیت مالی خطرناکی قرار دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000832785.mp3"},{"sentence":"a politically dangerous strategy","translation":"یک استراتژی خطرناک سیاسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001798969.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c4c8d10d-c989-5365-a06e-cfa87c5be71e','9ee47b14-88af-5b45-abda-69e9ac2edab3',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'dangerous ground/territory','خطرناک، پرمخاطره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('77635811-b28f-5224-9248-44d2ff992339','72cdeafa-08a5-59db-8a06-9fb7951bdc26',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a system of government in which every citizen in the country can vote to elect its government officials','[ uncountable ]',null,'دموکراسی، حکومت مردمی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a return to democracy after 16 years of military rule","translation":"بازگشت به دموکراسی پس از 16 سال حکومت نظامی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747807.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('514d83ae-d679-581d-8938-975ee84dfaee','72cdeafa-08a5-59db-8a06-9fb7951bdc26',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a country that has a government which has been elected by the people of the country','[ countable ]',null,'کشوری که دارای حکومتی است که توسط مردم کشور انتخاب شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a parliamentary democracy (= one with an elected parliament ) Britain is a parliamentary democracy.','a multiparty democracy (= with a number of political parties ) It is one of the few countries in the area that is a true multiparty democracy.','a Western democracy The sanctions are supported by all the major Western democracies.','a new democracy They are facing many of the same problems that all new democracies experience.','an emerging/fledgling democracy (= new ) the emerging democracies of Eastern Europe']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a parliamentary democracy","translation":"دموکراسی پارلمانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747808.mp3"},{"sentence":"Western democracies","translation":"دموکراسی های غربی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747811.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8b6d8624-90a9-5276-b7dd-366d046b8832','72cdeafa-08a5-59db-8a06-9fb7951bdc26',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation or system in which everyone is equal and has the right to vote, make decisions etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'وضعیت یا سیستمی که در آن همه برابر هستند و حق رای، تصمیم گیری و غیره دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"democracy within the trade unions","translation":"دموکراسی در اتحادیه های کارگری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747812.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1b29aec4-ffa0-511f-9803-72aaef5ca5bc','829da0a8-d749-5be4-bdf5-fc6967eaa794',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an act of leaving a place, especially at the start of a journey','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'خروج، حرکت؛ رفتن (از زندگی، شغل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sudden/abrupt (= done suddenly, without being planned ) I didn''t know how I was going to explain his abrupt departure to the others. Their departure seemed rather sudden.','a hasty/speedy departure (= done very quickly and suddenly ) I was surprised by her hasty departure.','a flight/train/coach departure I''m afraid your flight departure has been delayed.','delay somebody''s departure (= make it later ) I decided to delay my departure by a few days.','a departure date ( also date of departure ) You cannot make a change to your booking within six weeks of your departure date.','a departure time Do you know your exact departure time?','a departure point (= the place where you leave from ) Luxor is one departure point for boat trips down the Nile.','a departure gate (= an exit from an airport to get a particular flight ) It was a long walk with all our luggage to the departure gate.','a departure lounge (= a room at an airport where people wait before their flights leave )','the departures board (= a board showing the times of planes or trains ) I scanned the departures board for details of my flight.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I saw Simon shortly before his departure for Russia.","translation":"سایمون را کمی قبل از عزیمتش به روسیه دیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000817356.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was a delay in the departure of our plane.","translation":"در خروج هواپیمای ما تاخیر داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747950.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mozart’s departure from Paris in September 1778","translation":"خروج موتزارت از پاریس در سپتامبر 1778","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747953.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('446d257f-0e95-5788-82c4-7d34c9dee555','829da0a8-d749-5be4-bdf5-fc6967eaa794',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an act of leaving an organization or position','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'عمل ترک یک سازمان یا موقعیت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sudden/abrupt (= done suddenly, without being planned ) I didn''t know how I was going to explain his abrupt departure to the others. Their departure seemed rather sudden.','a hasty/speedy departure (= done very quickly and suddenly ) I was surprised by her hasty departure.','a flight/train/coach departure I''m afraid your flight departure has been delayed.','delay somebody''s departure (= make it later ) I decided to delay my departure by a few days.','a departure date ( also date of departure ) You cannot make a change to your booking within six weeks of your departure date.','a departure time Do you know your exact departure time?','a departure point (= the place where you leave from ) Luxor is one departure point for boat trips down the Nile.','a departure gate (= an exit from an airport to get a particular flight ) It was a long walk with all our luggage to the departure gate.','a departure lounge (= a room at an airport where people wait before their flights leave )','the departures board (= a board showing the times of planes or trains ) I scanned the departures board for details of my flight.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He refused to discuss his departure from the government.","translation":"او حاضر به بحث درباره خروجش از دولت نشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747957.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f2aaef79-4119-5650-8fe1-f1d71e124bbf','829da0a8-d749-5be4-bdf5-fc6967eaa794',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a flight , train etc that leaves at a particular time','[ countable ]',null,'پرواز، قطار و غیره که در یک زمان خاص حرکت می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sudden/abrupt (= done suddenly, without being planned ) I didn''t know how I was going to explain his abrupt departure to the others. Their departure seemed rather sudden.','a hasty/speedy departure (= done very quickly and suddenly ) I was surprised by her hasty departure.','a flight/train/coach departure I''m afraid your flight departure has been delayed.','delay somebody''s departure (= make it later ) I decided to delay my departure by a few days.','a departure date ( also date of departure ) You cannot make a change to your booking within six weeks of your departure date.','a departure time Do you know your exact departure time?','a departure point (= the place where you leave from ) Luxor is one departure point for boat trips down the Nile.','a departure gate (= an exit from an airport to get a particular flight ) It was a long walk with all our luggage to the departure gate.','a departure lounge (= a room at an airport where people wait before their flights leave )','the departures board (= a board showing the times of planes or trains ) I scanned the departures board for details of my flight.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are several departures for New York every day.","translation":"هر روز چندین حرکت به سمت نیویورک وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000817366.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0006abc5-2818-516d-b59e-4f969abf5af6','829da0a8-d749-5be4-bdf5-fc6967eaa794',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a way of doing something that is different from the usual , traditional , or expected way','[ countable ]',null,'روشی برای انجام کاری که با روش معمول، سنتی یا مورد انتظار متفاوت است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['sudden/abrupt (= done suddenly, without being planned ) I didn''t know how I was going to explain his abrupt departure to the others. Their departure seemed rather sudden.','a hasty/speedy departure (= done very quickly and suddenly ) I was surprised by her hasty departure.','a flight/train/coach departure I''m afraid your flight departure has been delayed.','delay somebody''s departure (= make it later ) I decided to delay my departure by a few days.','a departure date ( also date of departure ) You cannot make a change to your booking within six weeks of your departure date.','a departure time Do you know your exact departure time?','a departure point (= the place where you leave from ) Luxor is one departure point for boat trips down the Nile.','a departure gate (= an exit from an airport to get a particular flight ) It was a long walk with all our luggage to the departure gate.','a departure lounge (= a room at an airport where people wait before their flights leave )','the departures board (= a board showing the times of planes or trains ) I scanned the departures board for details of my flight.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Their new designs represent a departure from their usual style.","translation":"طرح های جدید آنها نشان دهنده انحراف از سبک معمول آنها است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747960.mp3"},{"sentence":"This would be a radical departure from the subsidy system.","translation":"این یک انحراف اساسی از سیستم یارانه خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000817374.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2f3b25bf-8ccc-5b3a-888d-745ee4b22ba1','ea26d7ac-89b0-53d8-a991-c23be1994a12',1,null,null,'spoken & written','needing someone or something in order to exist , be successful , be healthy etc',null,null,'وابسته، نیازمند (به)؛ زیرمجموعه (بستگان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Norway’s economy is heavily dependent on natural resources.","translation":"اقتصاد نروژ به شدت به منابع طبیعی وابسته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755635.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jan’s mother was dependent on her for physical care.","translation":"مادر جان برای مراقبت فیزیکی به او وابسته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755639.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do you have any dependent children (= who you are still supporting financially ) ?","translation":"آیا فرزندان وابسته ای دارید (= که هنوز از نظر مالی حمایت می کنید)؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001136103.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('0c427509-891e-5f9f-9013-6cb1496c4d07','ea26d7ac-89b0-53d8-a991-c23be1994a12',2,null,null,'spoken & written','addicted to drugs , alcohol etc',null,null,'معتاد به مواد مخدر، الکل و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the needs of people dependent on drugs","translation":"نیازهای افراد معتاد به مواد مخدر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755652.mp3"},{"sentence":"a danger of becoming alcohol dependent","translation":"خطر وابسته شدن به الکل","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755653.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('307c6da7-64dc-50c0-b614-afa0788cfa74','ea26d7ac-89b0-53d8-a991-c23be1994a12',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be dependent on/upon something','وابسته، نیازمند (به)؛ زیرمجموعه (بستگان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
