('060cf476-138f-52d0-8cbf-ddab9beb8f14','f4831234-94c3-55b9-b295-7608b14e1d31',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to become impossible to see any longer',null,null,'ناپدید شدن، محو شدن؛ رفته‌رنگ شدن',array['vanish']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The sun had disappeared behind a cloud.","translation":"خورشید پشت ابر ناپدید شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000826244.mp3"},{"sentence":"David watched her car until it disappeared from view.","translation":"دیوید ماشین او را تماشا کرد تا اینکه از دید ناپدید شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000826247.mp3"},{"sentence":"At this point the path seemed to disappear altogether (= disappear completely ) .","translation":"در این مرحله به نظر می رسید که مسیر به طور کلی ناپدید می شود (= کاملاً ناپدید می شود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000826241.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('3cc06b61-67a4-5770-bf4f-3c72563ab892','f4831234-94c3-55b9-b295-7608b14e1d31',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to be lost, or to become impossible to find',null,null,'گم شدن یا یافتن غیرممکن',array['vanish']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['simply disappear (= used to emphasize that it is very strange ) After two weeks it seemed that the boys had simply disappeared.','completely/totally disappear My spectacles have completely disappeared again.','mysteriously disappear (= in a way that no one can explain ) Several reporters in the area have mysteriously disappeared.','suddenly disappear The ship had suddenly disappeared in calm waters.','disappear without a trace ( also disappear without trace British English ) (= completely ) Hundreds of people disappear without trace every year.','disappear into thin air (= completely ) The money he made has disappeared into thin air.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The two girls disappeared while walking home from school.","translation":"این دو دختر در حالی که از مدرسه به خانه می رفتند ناپدید شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703767.mp3"},{"sentence":"My keys have disappeared again.","translation":"کلیدهای من دوباره ناپدید شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703768.mp3"},{"sentence":"75,000 soldiers simply disappeared without trace.","translation":"75000 سرباز بدون هیچ ردی ناپدید شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703775.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('db6ad8d8-3ee2-51a4-97c5-23844d1b7ffc','f4831234-94c3-55b9-b295-7608b14e1d31',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to stop existing',null,null,'برای متوقف کردن وجود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The rain forest may disappear forever.","translation":"جنگل بارانی ممکن است برای همیشه ناپدید شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000826251.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7d8ae2cd-bcc2-5da2-a65b-c838d512380f','e01a249b-c435-51ec-a508-e4b8f6b77a28',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a fact or thing that someone finds out about, when it was not known about before','[ countable ]',null,'کشف، اکتشاف؛ یافته (چیز تازه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a discovery By making new discoveries we expand our understanding of the natural world.','lead to a discovery It was pure chance that led to the discovery.','a new discovery New discoveries are being made all the time.','a recent discovery the recent discovery of frozen water on the moon','a great/major/important discovery The archaeologists had made an important discovery.','a scientific/medical etc discovery The book covers the major scientific discoveries of the last century.','an exciting discovery The existence of the new solar system was a very exciting discovery.','a surprising/unexpected discovery Their work led to some surprising discoveries.','a startling discovery (= very surprising ) When they examined the virus, they made a startling discovery.','an accidental/chance discovery (= happening by chance ) Some of the tombs were the result of chance discoveries.','a grim discovery (= an unpleasant and sad discovery such as finding a dead body ) Police made the grim discovery while they were searching the house.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Hubble Telescope allowed astronomers to make significant discoveries about our galaxy.","translation":"تلسکوپ هابل به اخترشناسان اجازه داد تا اکتشافات مهمی در مورد کهکشان ما انجام دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000465.mp3"},{"sentence":"the discovery that bees can communicate with each other","translation":"کشف این که زنبورها می توانند با یکدیگر ارتباط برقرار کنند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803506.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8e6a8666-8c87-55b7-98a8-ff5e5c86e6b9','e01a249b-c435-51ec-a508-e4b8f6b77a28',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when someone discovers something','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی کسی چیزی را کشف می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a discovery By making new discoveries we expand our understanding of the natural world.','lead to a discovery It was pure chance that led to the discovery.','a new discovery New discoveries are being made all the time.','a recent discovery the recent discovery of frozen water on the moon','a great/major/important discovery The archaeologists had made an important discovery.','a scientific/medical etc discovery The book covers the major scientific discoveries of the last century.','an exciting discovery The existence of the new solar system was a very exciting discovery.','a surprising/unexpected discovery Their work led to some surprising discoveries.','a startling discovery (= very surprising ) When they examined the virus, they made a startling discovery.','an accidental/chance discovery (= happening by chance ) Some of the tombs were the result of chance discoveries.','a grim discovery (= an unpleasant and sad discovery such as finding a dead body ) Police made the grim discovery while they were searching the house.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the discovery of oil in Alaska","translation":"کشف نفت در آلاسکا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000803513.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('be207e52-2d0f-5ad5-a7fe-c108d8afead5','c3c2ba82-2dae-548b-b578-1fcca7dd2e91',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the ship in which Captain Scott went to the Antarctic in 1901–04',null,null,'کشتی ای که کاپیتان اسکات در سال 1901-1904 با آن به قطب جنوب رفت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ca0a42e8-890c-5560-bd6d-e9e1cd1a82f7','4d766e59-aa68-5b7a-8238-5c3dfd991a32',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the study of the way in which money and goods are produced and used','[ uncountable ]',null,'اقتصاد (علم)؛ علم اقتصاد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a Harvard professor of economics","translation":"استاد اقتصاد هاروارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001641252.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3afc414c-0370-5e3d-a042-02eef3f87c56','4d766e59-aa68-5b7a-8238-5c3dfd991a32',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which money influences whether a plan, business etc will work effectively','[ plural ]',null,'روشی که از طریق آن پول بر عملکرد مؤثر یک طرح، تجارت و غیره تأثیر می گذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the economics of the scheme","translation":"اقتصاد طرح","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001181041.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3a359092-f12a-5926-b397-47a9a8d6f88a','5875a971-514a-5651-8a33-34d8dc1f9aef',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the process of teaching and learning , usually at school, college , or university','[ singular, uncountable ]','formal education','آموزش، تعلیم و تربیت؛ سواد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a good education All parents want a good education for their children.','a poor education (= not very good ) She had a poor education, and left school without qualifications.','an all-round education (= including a balance of lots of different subjects ) The school offers a good all-round education.','full-time education (= spending every weekday in a school or college ) Children must stay in full-time education until the age of 16.','state education British English , public education American English (= provided by the government of a country ) The state of California guarantees free public education to all children.','private education (= that people have to pay for ) I don''t agree with the principle of private education.','formal education (= from teachers at school or college, rather than learning by yourself ) She had no formal education and was brought up by her grandmother.','primary (school) education British English , elementary education American English (= for children aged between 5 and 11 ) The government has announced plans to improve the quality of primary school education.','secondary education ( also high school education American English ) (= for children aged between 11 and 18 ) She hopes to start a teaching career in secondary education.','university/college education Do you have a university education?','further/higher education (= at a college or university ) I did a carpentry course at the further education college.','adult education (= for adults ) They run adult education classes at the local community college.','vocational education (= relating to skills needed for a particular job ) We offer vocational education and job training.','nursery/pre-school education (= for children aged under 5 ) The funding will provide nursery education for all four-year-olds.','have an education The women have had little education.','get/receive an education Some children grow up without receiving any education.','give/provide an education The school aims to provide a good general education.','enter education (= start going to school, college etc ) The number of students entering higher education has risen.','leave education British English (= stop going to school, college etc ) She left full-time education at the age of 16.','continue your education I hope to continue my education after high school.','the education system (= the way education is organized and managed in a country ) Is the British education system failing some children?','the education department (= the government organization that makes decisions about education ) Newcastle City Council’s education department','an education authority (= a government organization that makes official decisions about education in one particular area ) The school is funded by the local education authority.','the education service (= all the government organizations that work together to provide education ) There are plans to expand the adult education service.','education policy (= political plans for managing an education system ) The teaching unions are calling for the government to review its education policy.','education reform (= changes that a government makes to the education system in a country ) the government’s programme of education reform']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She also hopes her children will get a good education.","translation":"او همچنین امیدوار است فرزندانش تحصیلات خوبی ببینند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001637621.mp3"},{"sentence":"efforts to improve girls’ access to education","translation":"تلاش برای بهبود دسترسی دختران به آموزش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000505.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
